# Migration Log: Dash → Vizro

## Phase A: Spike (decision gate) — 2026-06-03

| Item | Result |
|------|--------|
| Vizro version | 0.1.53 (within >=0.1.50 range) |
| Spike files | `dashboard/spike/app.py` (24 LOC), `dashboard/spike/custom_charts.py` (18 LOC) |
| Custom chart LOC | 18 — well under 50 LOC threshold |
| Build test | PASS — `Vizro().build(dashboard)` succeeds |
| Server test | PASS — http://localhost:7860 serves 16KB page, 200 OK |
| DuckDB wiring | PASS — `data_manager["key"] = lambda: load_mart(name)` works |
| `@capture("graph")` | Must be **called** with `data_frame=` arg, not passed as reference |
| Decision | **GO** — proceed to Phase C |

### Key Learnings
1. `@capture("graph")` returns `_DashboardReadyFigure` when called with string data_frame — must pass result to `vm.Graph(figure=...)`, not the function itself
2. `vm.Dropdown(options="all")` is invalid in 0.1.53 — options must be a list; use `vm.Filter(column=...)` without explicit selector for auto-generated filters
3. `data_manager["key"] = load_fn` (function ref) is the correct pattern for lazy evaluation

